# Tasks

Purpose:
  Task lifecycle engine. Defines how tasks are created, assigned,
  executed, reviewed, and closed within the SDDRA system.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @tasks.sdd (task lifecycle rules and contracts)

Rules:
  [T1] Every task MUST have a unique ID.
  [T2] Tasks MUST be assigned to specific stages.
  [T3] Task status MUST be tracked: pending -> active -> done.
  [T4] Task dependencies MUST be resolved before execution.

Navigation:
   Tasks: @tasks.sdd
   ProjectTasks: @../projects/{project_name}/tasks/INDEX.sdd
   TaskStateMachine: @TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
   LoopProtection: @LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd
   FailureClassification: @FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd
   ExecutionContract: @EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd
   AutonomyPolicy: @AUTONOMY-POLICY.sdd
   DoneProof: @DONE-PROOF.sdd
   PartialDone: @PARTIAL-DONE.sdd
   SkillChain: @SKILL-CHAIN.sdd
   TaskScheduling: @TASK-SCHEDULING.sdd
   ExecutionLoop: @../workflow/execution-loop.sdd
   LearningGate: @../workflow/learning-gate.sdd
   HumanDocsGate: @../workflow/human-docs-gate.sdd
   ExplainCommand: @../commands/sdd-explain.sdd
    Branches: @../branches/DOWN-UP-TRANSITION.sdd
    SDLC: @../branches/sdlc.sdd
    STLC: @../branches/stlc.sdd
    AdapterRuntime: @../runtime/adapter-runtime.sdd
    SecurityEnforcement: @../gates/security-enforcement.sdd

State: +
